{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Updated `/workspace/in/schema_migration/client.py`.\n\nProblem: converter only handled a partial v1 shape. It now supports v1, v1.1, v1.2, and idempotent v2 normalization.\n\nWhat changed:\n- `convert_order(payload)`\n  - Legacy mappings:\n    - `id`/`order_ref` → `orderId`\n    - `customer_id`/`customer.id` → `buyer.id`\n    - `customer_name`/`customer.name` → `buyer.displayName`\n    - `items`/`lines` → `lineItems`\n    - `qty` → `quantity` as `int`\n    - `price_cents`/`unit_price_cents` → `unitPriceCents` as `int`\n    - `ship_to.postal` / `ship_to.postalCode` / `shipTo.postal_code` → `shipping.address.postalCode`\n    - blank/null shipping method → `\"standard\"`\n  - Source tagging:\n    - `legacy-v1`, `legacy-v1.1`, `legacy-v1.2`, or preserved v2 `metadata.source`\n  - Unknown-field preservation:\n    - legacy extras preserved under `metadata.unknownFields`\n    - obvious PII-like keys dropped per `pii_policy.md`\n    - v2 `metadata.unknownFields` preserved\n    - extra v2 metadata fields folded into `metadata.unknownFields`\n  - v2 handling:\n    - no line-item rewrites beyond validation\n    - shipping method normalized only when blank/null\n\n- `convert_many(payloads)`\n  - aggregates conversion\n  - continues past bad records\n  - returns a compatible `ConversionResult`\n    - unpackable as `(converted, errors)`\n    - warnings available at `result[2]` and `result.warnings`\n  - error entries include `index`, `path`, `error`\n  - warning entries include `index`, `path`, `warning`\n  - writes `conversion_audit.json` next to `client.py`\n\n- CLI:\n  - `python3 -m client input.jsonl output.json`\n  - reads JSONL payloads\n  - writes converted records JSON\n  - writes `conversion_audit.json`\n  - exits nonzero if record errors occurred\n\nChecks:\n- `python3 -m py_compile client.py` — passed.\n- CLI smoke test:\n  - `python3 -m client sample_payloads.jsonl /tmp/schema_migration_output.json`\n  - wrote `/tmp/schema_migration_output.json`\n  - wrote `/workspace/in/schema_migration/conversion_audit.json`\n- Manual contract check in Python:\n  - replicated the provided test assertions for:\n    - v1 conversion\n    - default shipping normalization\n    - v2 passthrough/idempotence for `metadata.unknownFields`\n    - `convert_many` error aggregation\n    - v1.2 nested-field mapping and PII dropping\n  - also ran `convert_many` over `sample_payloads.jsonl`\n  - observed audit:\n    - `converted_count: 4`\n    - `error_count: 0`\n    - `warning_count: 5`\n    - `pii_dropped_count: 5`\n    - `unknown_fields_count: 5`\n\nPytest:\n- `python3 -m pytest /workspace/in/schema_migration/tests` could not run here because `pytest` is not installed: `/usr/bin/python3: No module named pytest`.\n- Given that environment limit, I verified the same behaviors directly against the module and exercised the CLI path."}}
